Summary: Don't fault in a system APC storing an async result into a status block that isn't writable
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c (invoke_system_apc); written for
 wine-mac-builds.
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: When an asynchronous read or write finishes, the APC_ASYNC_IO system
 APC stores the result in the caller's IO_STATUS_BLOCK (set_async_iosb). A
 thread that is running its own code gets system APCs through SIGUSR1, and
 runs them on the signal stack. If the status block is no longer writable
 memory, the store faults there; the fault can't be handled in a signal
 handler ("nested exception on signal stack"), and the thread never
 returns to its code. The status block can be freed by the program, or be
 on the stack of a thread that has exited, in which case the server gives
 the APC to any thread of the process. Windows ignores a status block it
 can't write. Now the result is stored with
 virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory, which checks the pages first, and is
 dropped with a warning if they aren't writable. Information is still
 written before Status, as set_async_iosb does.
Programs: Steam's updater (11.22 on macOS 15): after "Update complete,
 launching Steam..." a thread holding the loader lock stored a 32-bit
 status block into a reserved, uncommitted page and hung; every other
 thread then waited on the loader lock, so the updated Steam never started
Uncertain: the APC's callback can also write the program's buffer (a read's
 data); that isn't covered here, and didn't fault for Steam.
Evidence: A build12 ntdll.so that logs each SIGSEGV showed the fault, the
 first in the process: a write (err 0x6) at invoke_system_apc's
 set_async_iosb (server.c:419; movl %edx, 0x4(%rcx), the Information
 field of an IO_STATUS_BLOCK32) to 0x79ca5268, in a reserved page with
 reserved pages around it (vmmap). The same in two runs. Wine 10.0 has the
 same code; why Steam reaches it only on 11.x isn't known.
Applies to: wine 11.22 (macfixes, after 0066)
Status: 2026-11-19: not yet in a build. Tested by swapping a ntdll.so built
 with it into 11.22-build12 on meeka (macOS 26.7.2): async-iosb-decommitted
 passes (i686 and x86_64); without it both hang the reading thread, with
 the same "nested exception on signal stack" as Steam. The rest of the
 regression suite passes on that tree (screen-taking tests skipped). Not
 yet run with Steam.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -390,6 +390,43 @@
 
 
 /***********************************************************************
+ *              set_system_apc_iosb
+ *
+ * set_async_iosb for an APC_ASYNC_IO system APC, which may run in a signal
+ * handler (a thread running its own code gets system APCs through SIGUSR1),
+ * where a fault can't be handled. The status block may no longer be
+ * writable memory: a program can free it, or it was on the stack of a
+ * thread that has exited, and the server then gives the APC to any thread.
+ * Windows ignores a status block it can't write; so does this. Information
+ * is written before Status, as set_async_iosb does.
+ */
+static void set_system_apc_iosb( client_ptr_t iosb, NTSTATUS status, ULONG_PTR info )
+{
+    NTSTATUS ret;
+
+    if (!iosb) return;
+
+    if (in_wow64_call())
+    {
+        IO_STATUS_BLOCK32 *io = wine_server_get_ptr( iosb );
+        ULONG info32 = info;
+
+        if (!(ret = virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( &io->Information, &info32, sizeof(info32) )))
+            ret = virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( &io->Status, &status, sizeof(status) );
+        if (ret) WARN( "status block %p isn't writable; result %#x not stored\n", io, (int)status );
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        IO_STATUS_BLOCK *io = wine_server_get_ptr( iosb );
+
+        if (!(ret = virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( &io->Information, &info, sizeof(info) )))
+            ret = virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( &io->Status, &status, sizeof(status) );
+        if (ret) WARN( "status block %p isn't writable; result %#x not stored\n", io, (int)status );
+    }
+}
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
  *              invoke_system_apc
  */
 static void invoke_system_apc( const union apc_call *call, union apc_result *result, BOOL self )
@@ -416,7 +453,7 @@
             result->async_io.status = status;
             result->async_io.total = info;
             /* the server will pass us NULL if a call failed synchronously */
-            set_async_iosb( call->async_io.sb, result->async_io.status, info );
+            set_system_apc_iosb( call->async_io.sb, result->async_io.status, info );
         }
         else result->async_io.status = STATUS_PENDING; /* restart it */
         break;
